#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:6
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:8
msgid ""
"Dual-continuum (DC) model of a lithium-ion cell (Paten et al., 2026), built "
"as a subclass of `pybamm.lithium_ion.DFN`. The electrolyte, solid-phase "
"conduction, kinetics, thermal and lithium-metal counter-electrode physics "
"are identical to those in PyBaMM's DFN. The difference is the active "
"material (AM): instead of solving radial diffusion in idealised spherical "
"particles at every point of the electrode, the AM mass balance is "
"homogenised with the volume-averaging technique,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:16
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\frac{\\partial c_\\mathrm{vol}}{\\partial t} = -\\frac{a j}{\\varepsilon_s "
"F},\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:20
msgid ""
"where $c_\\mathrm{vol}$ is the volume-averaged AM concentration, $a$ the "
"specific surface area, $\\varepsilon_s$ the AM volume fraction and $j$ the "
"reaction rate. The surface-averaged concentration $c_\\mathrm{surf}$ used in "
"the kinetics is given by one of four definitions (Table I of Part I, and "
"Part II for DC1t):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/models/dual_continuum.md:5
msgid "`\"model type\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/models/dual_continuum.md:5
msgid "surface concentration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/models/dual_continuum.md:5
msgid "`\"DC1\"` (default)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/models/dual_continuum.md:5
msgid "$c_\\mathrm{surf} = c_\\mathrm{vol} + \\langle s \\rangle_A j$"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/models/dual_continuum.md:5
msgid "`\"DC1t\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/models/dual_continuum.md:5
msgid ""
"$c_\\mathrm{surf} = c_\\mathrm{vol} + \\langle s^t \\rangle_A \\star "
"\\partial_t j$ (transient closure, see below)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/models/dual_continuum.md:5
msgid "`\"DC0\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/models/dual_continuum.md:5
msgid "$c_\\mathrm{surf} = c_\\mathrm{vol}$"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/models/dual_continuum.md:5
msgid "`\"Yang\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/models/dual_continuum.md:5
msgid ""
"$c_\\mathrm{surf} = c_\\mathrm{vol} + \\gamma j$, with $\\gamma = "
"\\left(l_d^2/(6 l_k^2) - l_d/(2 l_k)\\right) l_k/(D F)$"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:32
msgid ""
"In DC1, $\\langle s \\rangle_A$ [mol.m-1.A-1] is the **closure variable**: "
"the surface average of the solution of a closure problem solved once on the "
"electrode microstructure (e.g. with the `solveclosure` tool, ref. 56 of the "
"paper). It depends only on the microstructure, not on operating conditions "
"or material properties (when non-dimensionalised). No assumption on particle "
"shape is made. With `\"calculate surface concentration a priori\": "
"\"true\"`, $j$ is replaced by its electrode average, which removes one "
"algebraic equation per mesh cell. This is only appropriate for galvanostatic "
"(constant-current) operation; see the DC options below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:42
msgid ""
"Yang and Tartakovsky's model (Yang and Tartakovsky, 2025) uses a boundary "
"layer of thickness $l_d = a_d \\sqrt{D t}$ (up to $l_k$) inside particles of "
"length scale $l_k$, taken from the particle radius parameter, with a fitting "
"parameter $a_d$."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:46
msgid ""
"The DC model is a fully macroscale description: it has no radial dimension. "
"Radial output variables (e.g. `\"Positive particle concentration "
"[mol.m-3]\"`) are the volume average broadcast in r; use `\"Positive "
"particle surface concentration [mol.m-3]\"` for the surface concentration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:52
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:54
msgid ""
"import pybamm\n"
"import pybamm_model_zoo as zoo\n"
"\n"
"DualContinuum = zoo.load(\"DualContinuum\")\n"
"\n"
"# Defaults: PyBaMM's DFN parameter set plus the DC parameters below\n"
"solution = pybamm.Simulation(DualContinuum()).solve([0, 3600])\n"
"\n"
"# Cathode half cell\n"
"model = DualContinuum({\"working electrode\": \"positive\"})\n"
"\n"
"# LG M50 cell with the parameters of Paten et al. (2026), Table IV\n"
"solution = pybamm.Simulation(\n"
"    DualContinuum(), "
"parameter_values=pybamm.ParameterValues(\"Paten2026_DC\")\n"
").solve([0, 3600])\n"
"\n"
"# Any parameter set written for the DFN (no DC parameters needed)\n"
"model = DualContinuum(\n"
"    dc_options={\"closure variable\": \"isolated sphere\", \"surface area\": "
"\"spherical\"}\n"
")\n"
"solution = pybamm.Simulation(\n"
"    model, parameter_values=pybamm.ParameterValues(\"Chen2020\")\n"
").solve([0, 3600])\n"
msgstr ""

