msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:91
msgid "`\"closure variable\"` sets how $\\langle s \\rangle_A$ is obtained:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:92
msgid "`\"dimensional\"`: read from the parameter set;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:93
msgid ""
"`\"dimensionless\"`: $s^\\ast$ is read from the parameter set and $\\langle "
"s \\rangle_A = s^\\ast L / (D F)$, with $L$ the electrode thickness;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:95
msgid ""
"`\"isolated sphere\"`: $\\langle s \\rangle_A = -R_\\mathrm{eff} / (5 D F)$, "
"the analytical solution of the closure problem for an isolated sphere of "
"radius $R_\\mathrm{eff}$. With it, DC1 coincides with PyBaMM's `\"quadratic "
"profile\"` particle for spherical geometry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:100
msgid ""
"$D$ is evaluated at the local volume-averaged concentration and temperature. "
"The choice is therefore not only one of units: with a diffusivity that "
"depends on concentration or temperature, `\"dimensional\"` holds $\\langle s "
"\\rangle_A$ fixed at the value of the closure solve, while "
"`\"dimensionless\"` and `\"isolated sphere\"` rescale it with "
"$D(c_\\mathrm{vol}, T)$. With a constant diffusivity, `\"dimensional\"` and "
"`\"dimensionless\"` give the same result. For DC1t the option also sets how "
"the mode time constants are given; see the *Transient closure (DC1t)* "
"section below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:109
msgid ""
"`\"calculate surface concentration a priori\": \"true\"` estimates $j$ from "
"the applied current, so it is only for galvanostatic (constant-current) "
"operation. The model raises an error with any `\"operating mode\"` other "
"than `\"current\"`. It cannot detect voltage, power or CV steps inside a "
"`pybamm.Experiment`, so do not combine the option with such steps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:114
msgid ""
"`\"surface area\"`: with `\"from image\"` (the default), the specific "
"surface area is built from areas measured on images of the microstructure; "
"see *Specific surface area from images* below. `\"spherical\"` uses $a = 3 "
"\\varepsilon_s / R$, as in the DFN."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:118
msgid ""
"`\"lithium foil surface porosity\": \"true\"` multiplies the exchange-"
"current density of the lithium foil by `\"Separator surface porosity\"`. "
"Some DNS codes include the separator surface porosity in the kinetics at the "
"foil, since the foil only reacts where it meets the separator's pores; turn "
"this on when comparing with such a DNS. Leave it off otherwise: a foil "
"exchange-current density taken from the literature is usually given per "
"geometric area, so it already includes the contact with the separator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:126
msgid "Transient closure (DC1t)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:128
msgid ""
"In DC1 the closure variable is its steady value. In the transient model of "
"Part II (Paten et al., 2026b) it depends on time, $\\langle s^t \\rangle_A(t)"
"$, starting from 0 and reaching the steady value $s_0$, and the surface "
"concentration involves a time convolution with the history of the reaction "
"rate:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:133
msgid ""
"\n"
"c_\\mathrm{surf} = c_\\mathrm{vol} + \\langle s^t \\rangle_A \\star "
"\\frac{\\partial j}{\\partial t}.\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:137
msgid "This model writes the closure variable as a sum of exponential modes,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:139
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\langle s^t \\rangle_A(t) = s_0 \\sum_m w_m \\left(1 - e^{-t/\\theta_m}"
"\\right), \\qquad \\sum_m w_m = 1,\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:143
msgid ""
"with weights $w_m \\ge 0$ and time constants $\\theta_m$. For each mode the "
"convolution is then exactly one ODE,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:146
msgid ""
"\n"
"c_\\mathrm{surf} = c_\\mathrm{vol} + s_0 \\sum_m w_m y_m, \\qquad\n"
"\\frac{\\mathrm{d} y_m}{\\mathrm{d} t} = \\frac{j - y_m}{\\theta_m}, \\qquad "
"y_m(0) = 0,\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:151
msgid ""
"where $y_m$ is an exponentially weighted average of the past reaction rate. "
"This holds for any current history, so constant-voltage holds, rests and "
"drive cycles need no special treatment, and the model runs directly from a "
"`pybamm.Experiment`. By default $j$ is the local reaction rate. With "
"`\"calculate surface concentration a priori\": \"true\"`, the modes are "
"driven by the electrode-averaged reaction rate instead, which reproduces the "
"piecewise-galvanostatic convolution of Part II (Eq. 25) and is only for "
"galvanostatic operation. Each mode adds one state per mesh cell (`\"Positive "
"electrode transient closure mode m [A.m-2]\"`); 8 modes on 20 cells is 160 "
"states, against 400 for a DFN with 20 radial points."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:162
msgid ""
"The weights are normalised by their sum, so the closure variable always "
"starts at 0 and tends to $s_0$, and DC1t reduces to DC1 when all time "
"constants are short. For an isolated sphere the exact closure variable is a "
"sum of exponentials (Paten et al., 2026c), and DC1t with enough modes "
"reproduces the Fickian DFN."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:168
msgid "How the modes are given depends on `\"closure variable\"`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:170
msgid ""
"`\"dimensional\"`: `\"Positive electrode transient closure weight m\"` and "
"`\"Positive electrode transient closure time constant m [s]\"`, for $m = 1, "
"\\dots, N$, with $s_0$ in `\"Positive electrode s0 surface average\"`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:173
msgid ""
"`\"dimensionless\"`: the same weights, and time constants `\"Positive "
"electrode transient closure time constant m dimensionless\"`, with $"
"\\theta_m = \\theta_m^\\ast L^2 / D$;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:176
msgid ""
"`\"isolated sphere\"`: built-in modes fitted to the transient solution for "
"an isolated sphere, scaled by $R_\\mathrm{eff}^2 / D$; no parameters are "
"needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:179
msgid ""
"$N$ is the `\"transient closure modes\"` option. The default parameter "
"values contain the isolated-sphere modes, so the default DC1t describes the "
"same cell as the Fickian DFN. With a concentration-dependent diffusivity, "
"the dimensionless and isolated-sphere time constants are scaled with "
"$D(c_\\mathrm{vol})$."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:185
msgid "Choosing the modes: `fit_transient_closure`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:187
msgid ""
"The helper fits the modes to your closure variable. Give it the times `t` as "
"a NumPy array, and the closure variable `s` either as an array of its values "
"at those times (for example read from the output of a closure solve on an "
"image) or as a Python function of time, which is then evaluated at `t`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:192
msgid ""
"import pybamm\n"
"import pybamm_model_zoo as zoo\n"
"from pybamm_model_zoo.dual_continuum import fit_transient_closure\n"
"\n"
"fit = fit_transient_closure(t, s, diffusivity=4e-14)  # t [s], s "
"[mol.m-1.A-1]\n"
"print(fit)  # modes, largest error and warnings\n"
"fit.plot()  # data and fit on a log time axis, with the error\n"
"\n"
"model = zoo.load(\"DualContinuum\")(\n"
"    {\"working electrode\": \"positive\"},\n"
"    {\"model type\": \"DC1t\", \"transient closure modes\": fit.n_modes},\n"
")\n"
"parameter_values.update(fit.parameter_values(\"Positive\"), "
"check_already_exists=False)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:208
msgid ""
"The time constants are spaced logarithmically (a constant ratio between "
"neighbours), because each mode only shapes $s(t)$ within about a factor of "
"ten in time around its time constant, while $s(t)$ changes over several "
"factors of ten. By default they run from a tenth of the first data time to a "
"third of the time at which $s$ reaches 99% of $s_0$, and the number of modes "
"is increased until the largest error is below `tolerance` (default 0.5% of "
"$s_0$). The weights come from a non-negative least-squares fit with $\\sum_m "
"w_m = 1$. As a rule of thumb, about two modes are needed for each factor of "
"ten between the shortest and the longest time constant: at the default "
"tolerance, the isolated sphere needs 8 modes when its time constants span "
"about four factors of ten (for example from 0.01 s to 100 s). Smoother "
"closure data can need fewer. Use `n_modes`, `tolerance` or "
"`time_constant_range` to change the choice, and `dimensionless=True` for "
"data scaled as $t D / L^2$ and $s D F / L$."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:223
msgid ""
"The helper checks the data and reports problems in `fit.warnings` (also "
"logged):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:226
msgid ""
"**Unresolved early times.** At short times every geometry responds like a "
"flat wall, $s \\approx -2 \\sqrt{t/D} / (\\sqrt{\\pi} F)$. Closure solves on "
"voxel meshes that report cell-centre values give early data far beyond this "
"limit (offset by about $-h/(2 D F)$, cell size $h$); the helper reports the "
"implied $h$. Prefer a finer mesh near the surface, or use "
"`fix_early_times=True`, which replaces the data before `resolved_after` "
"(default $10 h^2/D$) by the short-time limit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:233
msgid ""
"**Overshoot.** The modes cannot represent $s(t)$ overshooting its final "
"value, which usually means the closure solve is not converged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:236
msgid ""
"`isolated_sphere_closure(t, radius, diffusivity)` gives the analytical "
"closure variable of an isolated sphere."
msgstr ""

