#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:256
msgid ""
"During the discharge DC1t is within 3 mV RMS of the DNS. The transient "
"closure captures most of the relaxation that the steady closure misses. Each "
"model stops at its own 3.0 V cut-off, and DC1t stops 1.1 s before the DNS; "
"stopped at the DNS's end time instead, it agrees within 0.1 mV after 900 s. "
"The remaining difference early in the rest (about 60 mV at +10 s at equal "
"charge) is not explained by the offset of the closure data, and may come "
"from the nonlinear kinetics and open-circuit potential near full lithiation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:264
msgid "Specific surface area from images"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:266
msgid ""
"With `\"surface area\": \"from image\"`, the reactive specific surface area "
"of each electrode is"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:269
msgid ""
"\n"
"a = a_\\text{AM-electrolyte} + \\varepsilon^\\text{surf}_\\text{CBD} "
"a_\\text{AM-CBD}\n"
"+ \\varepsilon^\\text{surf}_\\text{sep} a_\\text{AM-separator},\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:274
msgid ""
"with each specific area (per unit electrode volume) measured on images of "
"the microstructure. The carbon-binder domain (CBD) and the separator are "
"effective media that contain electrolyte in their pores, so a reaction still "
"takes place at AM-CBD and AM-separator interfaces, albeit at a reduced rate. "
"The surface porosities $\\varepsilon^\\text{surf}_\\text{CBD}$ and $"
"\\varepsilon^\\text{surf}_\\text{sep}$ express that reduction: they are the "
"fraction of those interfaces in contact with electrolyte. **We recommend "
"setting each surface porosity equal to the corresponding volume porosity.**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:282
msgid ""
"An effective particle radius $R_\\mathrm{eff} = 3 \\varepsilon_s / a$ is "
"computed from the total area and reported as `\"Positive electrode effective "
"particle radius [m]\"`; it is the radius used by the isolated-sphere "
"closure. This is purely to simplify compatibility with PyBaMM's DFN class, "
"which this model builds on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:287
msgid "SEI and other DFN options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:289
msgid ""
"The DC model accepts PyBaMM's `\"SEI\"` options and the DFN's other options, "
"with their parameters, for example"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:292
msgid ""
"model = DualContinuum(\n"
"    {\n"
"        \"SEI\": \"reaction limited\",\n"
"        \"SEI film resistance\": \"distributed\",\n"
"        \"total interfacial current density as a state\": \"true\",\n"
"    }\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:302
msgid ""
"The last two options are what PyBaMM would otherwise derive from `\"SEI\"`; "
"giving them explicitly avoids relying on those derived defaults. With "
"`\"surface area\": \"from image\"`, the SEI grows on the same total specific "
"surface area $a$ as the main reaction, including the AM-CBD and AM-separator "
"contributions. Particle-size distributions and loss of active material are "
"not supported."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:308
msgid "Composite electrodes (several particle phases)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:310
msgid ""
"An electrode with several active materials, e.g. graphite and silicon, uses "
"PyBaMM's `\"particle phases\"` option, which also requires a `\"surface "
"form\"`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:313
msgid ""
"options = {\"particle phases\": (\"2\", \"1\"), \"surface form\": "
"\"algebraic\"}\n"
"model = DualContinuum(options, {\"model type\": \"DC1t\"})\n"
"parameter_values = "
"model.add_dc_parameters(pybamm.ParameterValues(\"Chen2020_composite\"))\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:319
msgid ""
"Each phase has its own volume-averaged concentration, closure variable and "
"modes, coupled to the other phases only through the electrolyte and the "
"solid potential, as in the DFN. As for PyBaMM's particle parameters, the DC "
"parameters of a composite electrode are prefixed by phase, e.g. `\"Primary: "
"Negative electrode s0 surface average\"` and `\"Secondary: ...\"`; those of "
"an electrode with a single phase are not. "
"`fit.parameter_values(\"Negative\", phase=\"secondary\")` writes the "
"prefixed names."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:327
msgid ""
"`add_dc_parameters` adds the DC parameters a set lacks, for every phase, "
"with the DFN-equivalent values listed below; it never overwrites a value "
"already in the set. PyBaMM's default set has no composite parameters, so for "
"a composite model `default_parameter_values` is the DFN's default set alone. "
"`\"calculate surface concentration a priori\"` needs a single phase, since "
"how the current splits between phases is not known a priori."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:334
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/models/dual_continuum.md:5
msgid "Parameter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/models/dual_continuum.md:5
msgid "Used when"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/models/dual_continuum.md:5
msgid ""
"`\"{Domain} electrode s0 surface average\"` [mol.m-1.A-1], the closure "
"variable $\\langle s \\rangle_A$"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/models/dual_continuum.md:5
msgid "DC1, `\"closure variable\": \"dimensional\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/models/dual_continuum.md:5
msgid ""
"`\"{Domain} electrode s0 surface average dimensionless\"` $s^\\ast$, with $"
"\\langle s \\rangle_A = s^\\ast L / (D F)$"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/models/dual_continuum.md:5
msgid "DC1, `\"closure variable\": \"dimensionless\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/models/dual_continuum.md:5
msgid ""
"`\"{Domain} electrode specific surface area from image (AM-electrolyte) "
"[m-1]\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/models/dual_continuum.md:5
msgid "`\"surface area\": \"from image\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/models/dual_continuum.md:5
msgid ""
"`\"{Domain} electrode specific surface area from image (AM-CBD) [m-1]\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/models/dual_continuum.md:5
msgid ""
"`\"{Domain} electrode specific surface area from image (AM-separator) "
"[m-1]\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/models/dual_continuum.md:5
msgid "`\"CBD surface porosity\"`, `\"Separator surface porosity\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/models/dual_continuum.md:5
msgid "`\"{Domain} electrode Yang fitting parameter\"` $a_d$"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/models/dual_continuum.md:5
msgid "Yang"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/models/dual_continuum.md:5
msgid "`\"{Domain} electrode transient closure weight m\"` $w_m$"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/models/dual_continuum.md:5
msgid "DC1t, `\"dimensional\"` or `\"dimensionless\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/models/dual_continuum.md:5
msgid ""
"`\"{Domain} electrode transient closure time constant m [s]\"` $\\theta_m$"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/models/dual_continuum.md:5
msgid "DC1t, `\"dimensional\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/models/dual_continuum.md:5
msgid ""
"`\"{Domain} electrode transient closure time constant m dimensionless\"` $"
"\\theta_m^\\ast$, with $\\theta_m = \\theta_m^\\ast L^2/D$"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/model_zoo/models/dual_continuum.md:5
msgid "DC1t, `\"dimensionless\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:349
msgid ""
"`default_parameter_values` is the DFN's default set (Marquis2019 for a full "
"cell, Xu2019 for a half cell) passed through `add_dc_parameters`, which adds:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:352
msgid ""
"AM-electrolyte areas equal to the DFN's $3 \\varepsilon_s / R$, no AM-CBD or "
"AM-separator contact, a separator surface porosity equal to the separator "
"porosity, and a CBD surface porosity of 0.5."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:355
msgid ""
"The closure variable set to the isolated-sphere value $-R/(5 D F)$ at the "
"reference state, so the defaults describe the same cell as the DFN's."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:357
msgid "A Yang fitting parameter of 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:358
msgid ""
"For DC1t, the isolated-sphere modes (weights, and time constants scaled by "
"$R^2 / D$ at the reference state)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:361
msgid ""
"`pybamm.ParameterValues(\"Paten2026_DC\")` and "
"`pybamm.ParameterValues(\"Paten2026_DFN\")` are the DC1 and DFN columns of "
"Table IV (an LG M50 cell, fitted to the 1C discharge of Chen et al. 2020), "
"on top of PyBaMM's Chen2020 set for all other values. The model zoo "
"registers these names, and `\"Paten2026_3D_NMC\"`, as PyBaMM parameter sets; "
"the functions in `parameter_sets` return the same values as plain "
"dictionaries. The electrolyte tortuosities are given both as tortuosity "
"factors and as the equivalent Bruggeman coefficients, so either `\"transport "
"efficiency\"` option gives the same result."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:371
msgid "Validation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:373
msgid ""
"Pinned by `tests/test_dual_continuum.py`, for a full cell (Marquis2019) and "
"a cathode half cell (Xu2019):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:376
msgid "DC0 reproduces DFN `\"uniform profile\"` (rtol 1e-7)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:377
msgid ""
"DC1 with the isolated-sphere closure variable reproduces DFN `\"quadratic "
"profile\"` (rtol 1e-7), as do the default parameters, with dimensional and "
"dimensionless closure variables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:380
msgid ""
"The image-based specific surface area and $R_\\mathrm{eff}$ follow the "
"formula above, and `\"lithium foil surface porosity\"` scales the foil "
"exchange current by the separator surface porosity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:383
msgid "Lithium in the active material is conserved to round-off."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:384
msgid ""
"In a half cell with AM-CBD and AM-separator areas, surface porosities and "
"the foil scaling, DC0, DC1 and DC1 a priori match reference voltages from "
"the standalone implementation used in the paper to within 10 µV (`tests/data/"
"standalone_reference.csv`, whose header records how it was generated)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:389
msgid ""
"Splitting the specific surface area into AM-electrolyte, AM-CBD and AM-"
"separator contributions gives the same result as the same total area."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:391
msgid ""
"The Table IV parameter sets give identical results with the Bruggeman and "
"tortuosity-factor transport options."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:393
msgid ""
"With PyBaMM's `\"SEI\"` options, DC1 with the isolated-sphere closure "
"variable reproduces the DFN with the `\"quadratic profile\"` particle (rtol "
"1e-7)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:395
msgid ""
"DC1t with the default (isolated-sphere) modes reproduces the Fickian DFN "
"with a fine radial mesh, within 0.5 mV for a constant-current discharge "
"(full and half cell) and within 1 mV and 0.1 mA through a constant-current, "
"constant-voltage and rest experiment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:399
msgid ""
"Composite electrodes: splitting the graphite of Chen2020_composite into two "
"identical phases reproduces the single-phase model (rtol 1e-7) for DC1, DC1t "
"and Yang; for graphite and silicon, DC1t with the isolated-sphere modes of "
"each phase reproduces PyBaMM's two-phase Fickian DFN within 1 mV."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:403
msgid ""
"DC1t's dimensional, dimensionless and isolated-sphere inputs agree; DC1t "
"tends to DC1 as the time constants go to zero; with the electrode-averaged "
"reaction rate it equals the galvanostatic convolution $c_\\mathrm{vol} + "
"\\langle s^t \\rangle_A(t) j$."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:406
msgid ""
"On the tomographic NMC electrode, DC1t with modes fitted to the closure data "
"matches the DNS within 3 mV RMS during discharge, and within 80, 25 and 5 mV "
"at 10, 100 and 900 s into the rest."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:409
msgid ""
"`fit_transient_closure` recovers known modes, meets its tolerance, and flags "
"unresolved early times and overshoot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:412
msgid "Citation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../packages/pybamm-model-zoo/src/pybamm_model_zoo/dual_continuum/README.md:414
msgid ""
"See `CITATION.bib`. Please cite Paten2026 when using this model, Paten2026b "
"(Part II) when using DC1t, and Yang2025 when using the Yang model; they are "
"registered automatically, so `pybamm.print_citations()` credits them after "
"use. Paten2026c shows the formal equivalence between DC1t and the DFN for "
"isolated spheres."
msgstr ""

